---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";

const bookingUrl = "https://calendar.app.google/VMSWBtEeNv131AxA6";

const measures = [
	{
		name: "Lead: reps",
		what: "Did you run the planned move instead of the old reaction?",
		who: "You",
		when: "Weekly, one line on your scoreboard",
	},
	{
		name: "Lead: disturbance",
		what: "How hard did the old reaction hit, 0–10?",
		who: "You",
		when: "Weekly, same line",
	},
	{
		name: "Lag: what others see",
		what: "How often do they see the problem, 1–5?",
		who: "Your boss, peers and direct reports",
		when: "Day 0 and day 90",
	},
];
---
<BaseLayout
	title="Work with me — Lead From The Hip"
	description="One problem at work, worked for ninety days, measured at both ends by the people who see you work. Occasional one-on-one coaching, bought by you."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="Engagements"
		standfirst="This isn't the front door — the Substack and the exercises are. But from time to time I take on someone who wants the full version: one problem at work, worked for ninety days, with numbers at both ends. You buy it, you own it, and nothing here replaces the reps you'd otherwise be running yourself."
	>
		If you want more. <span class="accent">Here's what that looks like.</span>
	</Hero>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<p class="text-ink measure mb-6">
			The sessions matter less than what you do between them. Most of the work is
			yours. My job is to point you at what's actually driving the problem, help you
			design the rep, and keep the score honest.
		</p>
		<a
			href={bookingUrl}
			class="inline-block bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
		>
			Book a call →
		</a>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">One problem. Ninety days. Numbers at both ends.</h2>
		<ol class="flex flex-col mb-6">
			<li class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-4 border-t border-rule">
				<span class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">Week 0</span>
				<div>
					<p class="font-medium text-ink mb-1">List your problems.</p>
					<p class="text-ink text-base measure">
						Write down every problem at work you want help with, and what you'd want
						instead of each. Then send the list to the people who see you work: your
						boss, your peers, your direct reports. Ask them two things:{" "}
						<em>If everything else stayed the same, which one change would make the
						biggest difference?</em> and <em>How often do you see this now?</em> You
						also take the Hogan Assessment, about an hour.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
			<li class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-4 border-t border-rule">
				<span class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">Week 1</span>
				<div>
					<p class="font-medium text-ink mb-1">Debrief and pick one.</p>
					<p class="text-ink text-base measure">
						Ninety minutes. We put your Hogan results next to what your people said and
						pick the one problem that is high impact and within your control. We break
						one real example down in A-B-C terms, design the rep, and set your weekly
						measures.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
			<li class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-4 border-t border-rule">
				<span class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">Weeks 3, 6 and 9</span>
				<div>
					<p class="font-medium text-ink mb-1">Check-ins.</p>
					<p class="text-ink text-base measure">
						Forty-five minutes each. We look at your scoreboard, dispute whatever
						belief got in the way, and adjust the rep. Email me any time in between.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
			<li class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[9rem_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-4 border-t border-b border-rule">
				<span class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">Week 12</span>
				<div>
					<p class="font-medium text-ink mb-1">Re-measure.</p>
					<p class="text-ink text-base measure">
						The same people answer the same question. We compare day 0 to day 90, and
						you decide what's next.
					</p>
				</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p class="text-ink font-medium measure">
			List everything. Work one thing at a time. The rest of the list waits for the
			next cycle.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">Two kinds of numbers.</h2>
		<p class="text-muted measure mb-6">
			You control the first kind. The second tells you whether it worked.
		</p>
		<dl class="md:hidden flex flex-col mb-6">
			{measures.map((m) => (
				<div class="py-4 border-t border-rule last:border-b">
					<dt class="font-medium text-ink mb-1">{m.name}</dt>
					<dd class="text-ink">{m.what}</dd>
					<dd class="text-muted text-sm mt-1">{m.who} · {m.when}</dd>
				</div>
			))}
		</dl>
		<table class="hidden md:table w-full text-left text-base border-collapse mb-6">
			<thead>
				<tr class="border-b border-rule-strong">
					<th class="py-3 pr-4"><span class="sr-only">Measure</span></th>
					<th class="eyebrow text-muted font-medium py-3 pr-4">What it is</th>
					<th class="eyebrow text-muted font-medium py-3 pr-4">Who reports it</th>
					<th class="eyebrow text-muted font-medium py-3">When</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody class="text-ink">
				{measures.map((m) => (
					<tr class="border-b border-rule">
						<th scope="row" class="font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top whitespace-nowrap">{m.name}</th>
						<td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">{m.what}</td>
						<td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">{m.who}</td>
						<td class="py-3 align-top">{m.when}</td>
					</tr>
				))}
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<div class="measure flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink">
			<p>
				The lead measures are your goal, because they're within your power. The lag
				measure is the proof — the gap between how you see yourself and how others
				describe you, narrowing or not.
			</p>
			<p>Your raters are asked twice. That's it.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">How it's priced.</h2>
		<p class="text-muted measure mb-6">
			Priced per ninety-day cycle, because the cycle is what ends in a measurement.
			Current rates are on the call.
		</p>
		<div class="overflow-x-auto">
			<table class="w-full text-left text-base border-collapse">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b border-rule-strong">
						<th class="py-3 pr-4 w-36 md:w-48"><span class="sr-only">Option</span></th>
						<th class="eyebrow text-muted font-medium py-3">What's included</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="text-ink">
					<tr class="border-b border-rule">
						<th scope="row" class="font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Debrief</th>
						<td class="py-3 align-top">
							Hogan Flash report, 90-minute debrief, your problem list. Credited toward a
							full cycle if you start within 30 days.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-rule">
						<th scope="row" class="font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Full cycle</th>
						<td class="py-3 align-top">
							Everything on this page: Hogan Flash report, debrief, three check-ins, rater
							baseline and re-measure, email support.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-rule">
						<th scope="row" class="font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Next cycle</th>
						<td class="py-3 align-top">The same, without a new Hogan — so it costs less.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="border-b border-rule">
						<th scope="row" class="font-medium py-3 pr-4 align-top">Full Hogan reports</th>
						<td class="py-3 align-top">The detailed HPI, HDS and MVPI reports, added at cost.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">The rep deposit.</h2>
		<div class="measure flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink">
			<p>
				Part of your first full cycle is a deposit on your own reps. Do the work and it
				comes back.
			</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-1">
				<li>Attend all three check-ins.</li>
				<li>Log reps on your scoreboard in at least 10 of the 12 weeks.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				What your raters say at day 90 has no bearing on it. You get it back for doing
				the work, not for the result — the work is within your power; what other people
				notice isn't. Finish the reps and your first cycle costs what every cycle after
				it does.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Payment</h2>
		<div class="measure flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink">
			<p>
				In full at signup, or half at signup and half at week six. Hogan fees are paid up
				front — I pay Hogan before your report runs.
			</p>
			<p>
				Payment comes first on purpose. It's the first commitment, and it keeps the day-90
				numbers honest: nobody has a reason to see progress that isn't there.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">What I won't do</h2>
		<ul class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink measure">
			<li>
				<strong>I won't sell you a type.</strong> You are not a color, a letter, or an
				animal. The assessment is a starting point for designing behavior, not an
				identity.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>I won't promise personality change.</strong> Dispositions are stable
				across adulthood. Anyone telling you otherwise is selling something. Behavior is
				trainable; that is what we work on.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>I won't provide therapy.</strong> This is behavioral coaching that
				borrows from Rational Emotive Behavior Therapy (REBT). If something clinical
				surfaces I will say so and refer you on.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>I won't report on you to anyone.</strong> Not to your manager, not to
				your HR team, not in aggregate. Your results are yours.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>I won't pay you for results.</strong> The deposit comes back for reps,
				never for ratings. The moment money rides on the numbers, the numbers stop
				meaning anything.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">FAQ</h2>
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-6 measure">
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">How much of my time does this take?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					About five hours with me across ninety days: the assessment (an hour), the
					debrief (ninety minutes), three forty-five-minute check-ins, and a closing
					review. The reps themselves are designed to cost under five minutes a week — if
					a rep needs a recurring block on your calendar, it has been designed wrong.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">What do I ask the people I work with?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					Two short asks, ninety days apart. At the start: which problem on your list
					matters most, and how often they see it now. At the end: how often they see it
					now. Ask three to five people who actually see you work. I give you the wording.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Does my employer find out?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					Not from me. Everything is commissioned by you and delivered to you. The only
					people who know are the ones you choose to ask.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">What if the ninety-day measure shows nothing changed?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					Then it shows nothing changed, and you find out from data instead of from a
					feeling. That is the point of including it. Your rep deposit doesn't depend on
					it.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Why pay up front?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					Because your commitment matters more than my sessions, and paying is the first
					one. It also means neither of us has a reason to want the numbers to look better
					than they are.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Which assessments do you use?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					The Hogan Assessment suite — the Hogan Personality Inventory (HPI), the Hogan
					Development Survey (HDS), and the Motives, Values, Preferences Inventory (MVPI).
					Certified directly by Hogan in 2020.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Do I retake the Hogan every cycle?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">
					No. Personality is stable, so a retest would tell you nothing new. That's why the
					next cycle costs less.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3 class="text-lg mb-1">Do you work with teams?</h3>
				<p class="text-ink text-base">Occasionally, and it is a different engagement. Ask.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<a
			href={bookingUrl}
			class="inline-block bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
		>
			Book a call →
		</a>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
